    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1OROUT",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 1, Y = NAND(NOT(C1), NOT(C2)) = C1 OR C2 = majority(A1, B1, C1) \u2014 copy 1 of 7: the ripple carry C2 fans out onto stage 2\u0027s 7 carry-in pins, one waveguide per pin, so the whole carry-OR subtree is duplicated per consumer; this copy feeds T2H2N1A.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_e2cf63a5920d4c54bfef5d350442a5dd",
        "IdGuid": "275e28d7-a4ea-4d65-a093-8304551cf4f1",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "0e9445c5-d325-43d5-b0ba-d8d2cef1c329",
          "91a9d586-dfdc-4047-9c02-2f9ab307e1ef",
          "50bc5ca5-717e-4c2f-a51d-88242f82709f",
          "66ae5da8-033e-4f12-920e-358b4c4ce771",
          "c29ea1ea-bd90-4e62-94c3-f7c52cc54d98",
          "06258cd1-bdd3-42e0-beca-6be5a3a01b84"
        ],
        "GridX": 0,
        "GridY": 0,
        "PhysicalX": 23200,
        "PhysicalY": 5300,
        "Rotation90CounterClock": 0,
        "ChildComponentIds": [
          "input_a_50ca4ce216b74b9c9db2ec33201b3d8f",
          "input_b_4c173698f0604a9d8a844cf19d7851a4",
